# SEO infrastructure

## Structured data stack

The site emits these JSON-LD schemas from `app/layout.tsx`:
- **WebSite** with `SearchAction` (sitelinks search box)
- **Organization** with logo and description
- **SoftwareApplication** with `featureList` (12 categories) and `aggregateRating`

Per-tool pages emit from `components/tool-page.tsx`:
- **WebApplication** with `isAccessibleForFree: true`
- **BreadcrumbList** matching visible breadcrumb nav
- **FAQPage** when `lib/faqs.ts` has entries for the tool
- **HowTo** when `lib/how-tos.ts` has entries for the tool (currently 10/61 tools)

Homepage (`app/page.tsx`) emits **ItemList** JSON-LD listing all tools.

Guide pages (`app/guides/[slug]/page.tsx`) emit **FAQPage** + **BreadcrumbList**.

Blog posts emit metadata via `lib/blog.ts`. Currently 30 posts.

## Metadata pipeline

- `lib/seo.ts` exports `pageMetadata()` and `toolMetadata()`.
- `toolMetadata()` passes `tool.id` as `pageId` — this enables hreflang via `lib/hreflang.ts`.
- Never call `toolMetadata()` without the tool having an `id` that matches `IndexableId`.
- `googleBot` directives are set in root layout: `max-image-preview: large`, `max-snippet: -1`.

## Hreflang

- `lib/hreflang.ts` generates reciprocal hreflang links for all published locales.
- English is unprefixed (`/word-counter`), other locales use `/{locale}/{localized-slug}`.
- `toolMetadata()` now automatically passes `pageId`, so all 61 tools emit hreflang.
- When adding a new tool, add it to `lib/tools.ts` — hreflang flows automatically.

## Server-rendered locale (`lang` attribute)

- `middleware.ts` detects locale from URL prefix and sets `x-locale` header.
- `app/layout.tsx` reads the header via `headers()` and sets `<html lang>` and `dir` server-side.
- Do NOT use client-side `useEffect` to set `document.documentElement.lang` — crawlers won't see it.
- `components/locale-head.tsx` exists as legacy but is no longer used in `app/[locale]/layout.tsx`.

## Content architecture

### Tool guides (`components/*-guide.tsx`)
- Every tool has a dedicated guide component (61 total).
- Minimum 60 lines with: "How it works", "Common use cases", "Tips & best practices", "Privacy".
- Guides are server components — no `"use client"`. Content is crawlable.
- When creating a new tool, always create a matching guide component.

### Category guides (`app/guides/[slug]/page.tsx`)
- 9 programmatic guide pages, one per category from `lib/guide-content.ts`.
- Each has educational intro (200+ words), 3-4 sections, FAQs with JSON-LD, tools grid.
- Linked from topic pages, footer, and sitemap.

### Blog (`lib/blog.ts`)
- 30 posts targeting long-tail queries, each 800-1200 words.
- Each post links to 2-3 relevant tools and includes FAQ section.
- Blog is localized: `app/[locale]/blog/` serves translated versions when available.

### Topic hubs (`app/topics/[topic]/page.tsx`)
- 9 category pages with overview copy, tool grid, and "Read the full guide" CTA.
- Currently English-only — localize when locale pages link to them.

## Sitemap (`app/sitemap.ts`)

- Reads from `lib/tools.ts`, `lib/browse.ts` (topics), `lib/guide-content.ts` (guides), and `lib/blog.ts`.
- Includes `lastModified` and `images` (OG image on homepage).
- Do not hand-maintain a parallel URL list.

## Security headers

- CSP, X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy, X-Frame-Options, Permissions-Policy set in `next.config.ts`.
- `poweredByHeader: false`.

## Checklist for new tool pages

1. Add tool to `lib/tools.ts` with unique `id`, `title`, `metaDescription`, `primaryQuery`
2. Create `app/{slug}/page.tsx` using `toolMetadata(tool)` + `ToolPage` wrapper
3. Create `components/{slug}-guide.tsx` (60+ lines, server component)
4. Add FAQs in `lib/faqs.ts` (at least 2 Q&As)
5. Add HowTo in `lib/how-tos.ts` if the tool has clear steps
6. Add to `tool.related` on 2-3 existing tools
7. Sitemap, hreflang, and blog index update automatically
